# Chronology note

Before the reply, read `skills/record-chronology/SKILL.md` and `skills/record-chronology/references/note.md`.

When this turn changed the project or reached a result, put one chronology block in thinking, as `skills/record-chronology/SKILL.md` shows. Do not wait to be asked. Do not create or edit files in the chronology folder. The hook writes the note. A question that did not change the project and did not reach a result writes nothing and puts no block in thinking.

Do not write the transcript. Do not write a secret, a token, or the contents of an env file. The same window keeps the same file. At most two sections per UTC day. A missing `git config user.name` skips the note and does not invent a folder.

The reply is only what was asked. It does not mention the note, the path, or a status line. When the person asked for the chronology note, the reply is the one line in the skill.
